How it works and what it relies on
----------------------------------

Ring Intercom Plus has no login of its own. It runs next to the official Home Assistant
Ring integration (https://www.home-assistant.io/integrations/ring/) and sends its
requests through that integration's authenticated client from the library
python-ring-doorbell (https://github.com/python-ring-doorbell/python-ring-doorbell,
GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0). Neither the library nor any of its source
files is included in or copied into this repository; Home Assistant installs it
for the Ring integration.

The request format of the door unlock command (door_id 0, user_id -1) follows
python-ring-doorbell. The other commands and settings (active call, hardware
revision, auto unlock, Ring-to-Open, unlock duration, reboot) were observed in the
official Ring app. The ding and unlock hold times (20 s and 5 s) follow the
behaviour of ring-mqtt (https://github.com/tsightler/ring-mqtt, MIT License), so
users switching over keep the same behaviour. No source files of ring-mqtt were
copied.

Unofficial API
--------------

Ring does not publish or support the interface used by this integration. Ring can
change it at any time, and single functions may stop working until this
integration is adapted.

